  "id": "DrugBank_DB00768 - MONDO_6004",
  "verbalization": "Olopatadine is suggested to be related to Vasomotor Rhinitis through a chain of indications involving Quifenadine and Acrivastine. The evidence shows that Olopatadine is associated with Atopic Conjunctivitis and Papillary Conjunctivitis, both of which are linked to Quifenadine, which in turn is linked to Vasomotor Rhinitis. This suggests a potential pathway where Olopatadine may exert effects on the conjunctiva, possibly through similar mechanisms to Quifenadine, leading to symptoms of vasomotor rhinitis. The shared indication chain between Olopatadine and Quifenadine implies a possible mechanistic overlap, though the exact nature of this relationship remains unclear. The evidence supports a possible repurposing of Olopatadine for vasomotor rhinitis, but further research is needed to confirm the direct causal link.",
